---js
{
  layout: 'base.njk',
  title: 'Lingua Magna: Don\'t just learn a language. Master it.',
  description: 'Don\'t just learn a language. Master it. Free courses in 7 languages: each lesson unlocks once you master what it builds on, and spaced review keeps it fresh.',
  kind: 'WebPage',
  eleventyComputed: {
    faqs: () => [
      { q: 'What is mastery-based learning?', a: 'You move on only after you prove you know something: a run of quick, correct answers. Lessons unlock when the ones they build on are mastered, and spaced review brings each word back right before you would forget it.' },
      { q: 'Which languages can I learn?', a: 'Mandarin Chinese (HSK 1 and 2), Spanish (2,000 words, A1 to B1), French, Italian, Portuguese and German (600 words each), and English for speakers of Spanish, Portuguese and Chinese.' },
      { q: 'Is it free?', a: 'Yes, all of it: lessons, word pages, audio and practice. Lingua Magna is open source and built from openly licensed data.' },
      { q: 'Do I need an account?', a: 'No. Just start. Your progress saves automatically in your browser.' },
      { q: 'How is my progress saved?', a: 'On your device, in your browser storage. Nothing is sent to a server. To switch devices, use Export progress in the practice settings and import the file on the other device.' },
      { q: 'Does it work on my phone?', a: 'Yes. It is built for phones first and runs in any modern browser, including Safari on iPhone. Add it to your home screen for an app-like feel. Lessons need an internet connection to load.' },
      { q: 'How is the audio made?', a: 'Native speakers first: real recordings from open projects like Lingua Libre, Wikimedia Commons and Tatoeba, wherever the license allows. The rest uses the clearest open-source voice for each language, chosen by testing every candidate with speech recognition.' },
      { q: 'Can I learn English from Spanish, Portuguese or Chinese?', a: 'Yes. Pick the language you speak when you start, and translations, grammar notes and the app itself switch to it.' },
      { q: 'I found a wrong word or translation. How do I report it?', a: 'Open a quick Data fix report on GitHub with the word and what it should say. Fixes ship to everyone on the next update.', link: { repo: '/issues/new/choose', text: 'Report a problem' } },
      { q: 'Can I contribute?', a: 'Yes. Code is MIT and content is CC BY-SA 4.0. Fix a meaning, write a grammar lesson or add a whole new language.', link: { repo: '/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md', text: 'How to contribute' } },
    ],
    ldItems: data => data.lm.packs.map(p => ({ name: `Learn ${p.adj}`, url: p.hubUrl })),
  }
}
---
{% set d0 = demo.langs[0] %}{% set q0 = d0.qs[0] %}
<section class="hero"><h1>Don't just learn a language. <em>Master it.</em></h1>
<p class="lead">Bite-sized lessons in 7 languages. Free, no account.</p>
<p class="cta"><a class="btn primary big" href="/learn/">Start learning free</a></p>
<div class="demo" id="demo" aria-label="Try a 3-question lesson">
<div class="dlangs" role="group" aria-label="Demo language">{% for l in demo.langs %}<button type="button" data-l="{{ l.id }}" aria-pressed="{{ 'true' if loop.first else 'false' }}">{{ l.name }}</button>{% endfor %}</div>
<div class="dtop"><div class="bar" aria-hidden="true"><i style="width:0%"></i></div><span class="xp" aria-label="XP">{% include "i-bolt.njk" %}<span class="n">0</span></span></div>
<div class="dcard" aria-live="polite"><div class="dq"><div class="i">Tap the meaning</div><div class="w" lang="{{ d0.id }}">{{ q0.w }}<button class="say" type="button" aria-label="Listen" data-say="{{ q0.w }}" data-lang="{{ d0.speech }}" data-a="{{ d0.audio }}">{% include "i-say.njk" %}</button></div><div class="r">{{ q0.r }}</div></div>
<div class="dch">{% for c in q0.choices %}<button class="choice" type="button">{{ c }}</button>{% endfor %}</div></div>
<script type="application/json" id="demo-data">{{ demo.langs | json | safe }}</script>
</div></section>
<section class="reveal"><h2>Real sentences, real people</h2>
<div class="carousel" id="cards">{% for c in demo.cards %}<article class="exc"><span class="lang">{{ c.name }}</span><span class="s" lang="{{ c.id }}">{{ c.t | hl(c.w) | safe }}</span><button class="say" type="button" aria-label="Listen" data-say="{{ c.t }}" data-lang="{{ c.speech }}" data-a="{{ c.id | apath('d:' + c.id) }}">{% include "i-say.njk" %}</button><span class="tr">{{ c.tr }}</span><a class="word" href="{{ c.url }}">{{ c.w }}{% if c.r %} · {{ c.r }}{% endif %} →</a><span class="credit">Tatoeba: {{ c.by }}</span></article>{% endfor %}</div>
<div class="dots" id="dots" aria-hidden="true"></div></section>
<section class="reveal"><h2>Pick a language</h2><div class="langgrid">{% for p in lm.packs %}{% set dl = demo.byLang[p.id][0] %}<a class="lg" href="{{ p.hubUrl }}"><span class="big" lang="{{ p.id }}">{{ dl.w if dl else p.short }}</span><b>{{ p.adj }}</b><span>{{ p.counts.words }} words{% if p.id == 'en' %} · for es, pt, zh{% endif %}</span></a>{% endfor %}</div></section>
<section class="reveal"><h2>How it works</h2><ol class="how">
<li><span class="ic" style="background:var(--gold2)">🎯</span><div><b>Find your level</b><span>Skip what you know.</span></div></li>
<li><span class="ic" style="background:var(--brand2)">🔓</span><div><b>Master to unlock</b><span>Next lesson opens when you nail this one.</span></div></li>
<li><span class="ic" style="background:var(--accent2)">🔁</span><div><b>Review just in time</b><span>Words come back before you forget.</span></div></li></ol></section>
{% include "faq.njk" %}
{% updated %}
